iner\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540616-aquatic-mages?p=1540645#post1540645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aw, I was actually kind of looking forward to speculating on an aquatic MtA game. (I'd have suggested looking at Blood-Dimmed Tides. Maybe there's something there that could be converted to nWod?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I can't help you on the aquatic MtAs front, since I don't really know OWoD Mage lore, but Blood-Dimmed Tides was a major source of hard and fast rules for scuba diving (which I, sadly, have never yet had the opportunity to attempt). I incorporated a bit of the lore from BDT into Tenebrous Seas, but a lot of elements like the Rorqual are just a bit too 90s for the modern day, y'know? But I did cite it as a source and encouraged readers to check it out. <br /> <br /> Actually I'm working on a mage antagonist to round out the doc before I put it up on storytellers vault. He's basically an ecoterrorist who's using global warming to fight global warming by creating city-killing hurricanes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Motor City Breakdown</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19D2lK7otRprpHsJz0aZF0WucpMtoEgGQ2ExZJ-ud0a4/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night in the D</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uFgCI8m4gJ5kg1DneG0Cgu18bmUpe4RxDNDfI824G6M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">The Magical History Tour</